WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:06.550
2019 may seem like it's a long way off, but
movie studios are already filling up their

00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:11.849
slates with big-budget, high-octane adventures
that theatergoers are not going to want to

00:00:11.849 --> 00:00:12.849
miss.

00:00:12.849 --> 00:00:17.040
While some may say it's a bit early for people
to be setting their calendar for midnight

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:20.950
release dates, we say that you can never plan
too much ahead.

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:22.800
You might even get some sweet merch!

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:26.400
"Star Wars fans brave the cold, long lines,
and traffic.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.710
The first one thousand people got an exclusive
Rogue One poster!"

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:37.010
So pop all your popcorn and clear space on
the wall for all your sweet new posters...here

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:40.289
are all the movies that will blow you away
in 2019.

00:00:40.289 --> 00:00:43.140
The Lego Movie Sequel

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:50.500
The first Lego Movie was the surprise hit
of 2014, making $469 million worldwide and

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:55.960
spawning a host of spin-offs, including the
Lego Batman movie, which made over $300 million

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:57.879
worldwide in 2017.

00:00:57.879 --> 00:01:03.280
However, the actual sequel to the original
film has run into some production delays,

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:06.480
pushing its release back to February 2019.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:07.640
One of the reasons for the hold-up?

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:11.600
A script rewrite from BoJack Horseman creator
Raphael Bob-Waksberg.

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:15.189
Now that we can't wait to see.

00:01:15.189 --> 00:01:17.320
How to Train Your Dragon 3

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:23.090
Check out the intense logline for How to Train
Your Dragon 3: "As Hiccup fulfills his dream

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:29.189
of creating a peaceful dragon utopia, Toothless'
discovery of an untamed, elusive mate draws

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:31.119
the Night Fury away.

00:01:31.119 --> 00:01:36.859
When danger mounts at home and Hiccup's reign
as village chief is tested, both dragon and

00:01:36.859 --> 00:01:41.070
rider must make impossible decisions to save
their kind."

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:46.290
Oscar-nominated writer and director Dean DeBlois
says the third movie in the franchise, set

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:51.710
for release in March 2019, will be the "culmination
of Hiccup's coming of age.”

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:58.219
So expect the movie to tie the whole franchise
together in one epic conclusion.

00:01:58.219 --> 00:02:00.210
Captain Marvel

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:05.579
Marvel's first female-led superhero film,
pegged for March 2019, is shaping up to be

00:02:05.579 --> 00:02:06.640
worth the wait.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:11.870
For one thing, Captain Marvel has Oscar winner
Brie Larson as its lead, an actress who's

00:02:11.870 --> 00:02:16.340
shown she has the ability to pull off action,
comedy, and drama.

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:21.980
And for another, Marvel enlisted the directing
team of Anna Boden and Ryan Fleck, who previously

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:26.680
helmed cult hits Half-Nelson and It's Kind
of a Funny Story.

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:32.090
Add in the promise from Marvel head honcho
Kevin Fiege that Captain Marvel will be "as

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:37.129
powerful a character as we've ever put in
a movie" and you have the recipe for yet another

00:02:37.129 --> 00:02:39.450
winner from Marvel Studios.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:42.069
Godzilla: King of Monsters

00:02:42.069 --> 00:02:48.160
Another March release, King of Monsters is
the follow-up to the well-received 2014 Godzilla.

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:50.900
But that's where the similarities apparently
end.

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:56.010
Other than returning star Ken Watanabe, the
movie is slated to bring in a whole new cast

00:02:56.010 --> 00:03:01.130
of human characters, with Vera Farmiga, Kyle
Chandler, and Stranger Things star Millie

00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:05.409
Bobby Brown playing a family swept up in the
trouble the monster causes.

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:07.720
Sorry, Godzilla, but we're betting on Eleven...

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:12.840
“Ah!

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:15.740
She broke my arm!

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:16.680
My arm!”

00:03:16.689 --> 00:03:17.970
“Go.”

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:19.260
Shazam!

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:24.940
It's been a long time in the making, but the
long awaited Shazam! movie from DC is currently

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:28.769
slated to finally hit theaters in April 2019.

00:03:28.769 --> 00:03:34.379
Although Warner Bros. has yet to announce
a lead, Shazam! promises to bring a new, lighter

00:03:34.379 --> 00:03:38.269
tone to DC's otherwise pretty grim film universe.

00:03:38.269 --> 00:03:43.500
Whether or not Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson will
appear as Black Adam remains to be seen, as

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:47.470
Shazam's archenemy has already had his own
solo film greenlit.

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:52.519
Either way, it'll be nice to see a DC film
where at least one scene takes place during

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:54.140
daylight hours.

00:03:54.140 --> 00:03:55.200
"Shazam!"

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:05.299
Fast &amp; Furious 9

00:04:05.299 --> 00:04:10.120
Vin Diesel teased the release date for the
ninth and tenth films in the Fast and the

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:15.580
Furious franchise on his Instagram before
The Fate of the Furious even had its official

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:16.580
name.

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:22.720
And with the eighth movie tearing up the box
office in 2017, the ninth is sure to be huge.

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:27.910
Considering the Fate of the Furious purposely
left some loose ends dangling, it seems as

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:34.310
though the stage is already being set to make
Fast &amp; Furious 9 the fastest and most furious

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:35.310
film yet.

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:37.810
If that's even possible.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.460
Avengers 4

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:45.880
In May 2019, the fourth Avengers film will
mark the end of Marvel's Phase 3, which means

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:48.070
it's probably time to break out your tissues.

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:52.729
With the first wave of Marvel film franchises
coming to an end — and with many of the

00:04:52.729 --> 00:04:58.380
big-name actors' contracts expiring as well
— Avengers 4 will probably result in quite

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:00.640
a few character deaths or retirements.

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:05.900
We'll learn a lot more about what to expect
in Avengers 4 when Avengers: Infinity War

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:07.690
hits theaters in 2018.

00:05:07.690 --> 00:05:12.210
But the movie is sure to be a can't-miss adventure.

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:14.210
Star Wars: Episode IX

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:20.320
Jurassic World's Colin Trevorrow will take
on directing duties for the as-yet-untitled

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:26.120
final film in the third Star Wars trilogy,
currently slated for a may 2019 release.

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:33.210
And if the past films have been any indication,
this one is going to be epic. 2017's The Last

00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:38.690
Jedi should tell us a lot about the plot of
Star Wars: Episode IX, but we do know that

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:43.620
it'll provide a resolution to the trilogy,
according to Lucasfilm president Kathleen

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:44.620
Kennedy.

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:49.050
And, if just the plot of the movie isn't enough
to get you out to the theaters, the studio

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:54.710
is looking to set up a future of standalone
movies and spinoffs — meaning Episode IX

00:05:54.710 --> 00:06:00.840
will probably be yet another launching pad
for years of the Star Wars franchise's future.

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:02.539
May it never end.

00:06:02.539 --> 00:06:04.139
Toy Story 4

00:06:04.139 --> 00:06:09.569
If you somehow didn't empty your tear ducts
forever during Toy Story 3, Toy Story 4 will

00:06:09.569 --> 00:06:11.400
arrive in June 2019.

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:16.759
According to Pixar chief creative officer
and Toy Story director John Lasseter, the

00:06:16.759 --> 00:06:21.849
treatment for the film, was "unbelievable,"
focusing on the love story between Woody and

00:06:21.849 --> 00:06:26.229
Bo Peep and showing Woody and Buzz teaming
up to find a missing Bo.

00:06:26.229 --> 00:06:31.270
The movie also has big names behind it, with
Lasseter set to co-direct alongside Inside

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:37.199
Out writer Josh Cooley, and a script by Celeste
&amp; Jesse Forever duo Rashida Jones and Will

00:06:37.199 --> 00:06:38.199
McCormack.

00:06:38.199 --> 00:06:39.660
“I’m Rashida Jones.”

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:41.040
“I’m Will McCormack.

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:44.750
And we are currently at Pixar writing Toy
Story 4.”

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:50.440
The Pixar machine hasn't failed us yet, and
we're excited to see their animated rom-com

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:52.080
on screen.

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:53.400
Transformers 7

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:57.690
Don't look now, but there's yet another Transformers
movie coming out!

00:06:57.690 --> 00:07:02.410
Actually, there's two, as Transformers 8 has
already been announced too, with several more

00:07:02.410 --> 00:07:04.800
spinoffs and sequels in development.

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:10.319
Just what will happen in June 2019's Transformers
7 is a closely guarded secret.

00:07:10.319 --> 00:07:15.360
But we're going to give you an exclusive right
now: it will involve CGI robots punching each

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:18.330
other until your eyes and ears bleed motor
oil.

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:20.099
The only thing that could be better?

00:07:20.099 --> 00:07:25.199
If someone figured out how to combine the
franchise with Fast &amp; Furious so all those

00:07:25.199 --> 00:07:28.720
autobots were being driven by Vin Diesel and
Ludacris.

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:31.289
Hey, we can dream, can't we?

00:07:31.289 --> 00:07:33.330
The Secret Life of Pets 2

00:07:33.330 --> 00:07:38.490
The original Secret Life of Pets flooded movie
theaters with adorableness in the summer of

00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:39.620
2016.

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:45.460
And although the sequel has been pushed back
to July 2019 from its originally planned 2018

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:48.460
release date, there are still a lot of good
things going for it.

00:07:48.460 --> 00:07:52.889
Set to follow the continuing adventures of
New York City's craziest pets, the sequel

00:07:52.889 --> 00:07:56.520
will bring back the writing and directing
team from the original.

00:07:56.520 --> 00:08:02.000
That means it should also be able to bring
back the magic that made the first film so

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:03.000
great.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:05.979
“The revolution has begun!

00:08:05.979 --> 00:08:07.569
Liberated forever!

00:08:07.569 --> 00:08:09.160
Domesticated never!

00:08:09.160 --> 00:08:10.160
Yeah!”

00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:11.759
Spider-Man: Homecoming 2

00:08:11.759 --> 00:08:16.470
Tom Holland's Spider-Man is set to continue
his adventures in a second standalone film

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:18.379
in July 2019.

00:08:18.379 --> 00:08:22.840
It should follow another year of Peter Parker's
high school experience, similar to the annual

00:08:22.840 --> 00:08:25.030
installments of Harry Potter.

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:29.979
While we've already seen plenty of Spider-Man
films, Holland's version promises to be different

00:08:29.979 --> 00:08:31.300
in a number of ways.

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:36.271
For one thing, if what Holland says is true
about the sequel staying in high school, it

00:08:36.271 --> 00:08:41.790
will be the only Spider-Man film iteration
to remain there for more than one movie.

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:46.220
That way, it can mine new story ideas that
other films have breezed past.

00:08:46.220 --> 00:08:50.200
There are lots of possibilities for Holland's
Peter Parker, and it should be interesting

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:53.340
to see what webs the filmmakers spin.

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:54.480
The Lion King

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:59.850
Disney's remake machine is already going strong,
and Jon Favreau's live-action version of The

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:05.480
Lion King, set to ascend to the throne in
July 2019, is expected to be huge.

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:10.710
The movie will bring back James Earl Jones
to reprise his role as Mufasa from the original,

00:09:10.710 --> 00:09:13.500
with Donald Glover providing the voice of
Simba.

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:18.010
And those stars already have some equally
impressive backup in the form of Seth Rogen

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:21.140
and Billy Eichner, who will voice Timon and
Pumba.

00:09:21.140 --> 00:09:26.190
Given how well Favreau's live action Jungle
Book adaptation turned out, this is one you

00:09:26.190 --> 00:09:28.370
won't want to miss.

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:29.550
Frozen 2

00:09:29.550 --> 00:09:34.770
Bundle up, because Frozen 2 is coming your
way in November 2019.

00:09:34.770 --> 00:09:39.010
Not much is known right now about the sequel
to the 2013 mega-hit.

00:09:39.010 --> 00:09:43.780
But we're ready to guarantee it will feature
at least a couple catchy songs that are sure

00:09:43.780 --> 00:09:47.900
to become karaoke mainstays for the rest of
eternity.

00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:53.050
The sequel will further explore the relationship
between Idina Menzel's Elsa and Kristen Bell's

00:09:53.050 --> 00:09:57.670
Anna, two of Disney's most engaging and feminist
heroines to date.

00:09:57.670 --> 00:10:02.400
So while we don't know anything specific about
the plot yet, we can guarantee that Frozen

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:05.200
2 is sure to warm your cold heart.

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:06.920
Oh, and also:

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:08.660
"Let it go!

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:09.860
Let it go!

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:14.320
I am one with the wind and sky!

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:15.380
Let it go!

00:10:15.520 --> 00:10:16.520
Let it go!”

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:18.840
Just when you finally got that out of your
head!

00:10:19.480 --> 00:10:20.480
Sorry.

00:10:20.940 --> 00:10:21.940
Masters of the Universe

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:29.500
Despite losing McG as its director, the December
2019 Masters of the Universe live action film

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:34.670
is still shaping up to be a powerhouse thanks
to the writing of David S. Goyer, the guy

00:10:34.670 --> 00:10:38.690
behind Batman Begins, The Dark Knight, Blade,
and more.

00:10:38.690 --> 00:10:43.710
There are also a lot of A-list actors reportedly
vying to play roles in the film.

00:10:43.710 --> 00:10:49.360
With more stars scrambling to sign on to superhero
movies in recent years, it looks like Masters

00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:55.250
of the Universe should have no problem assembling
an impressive cast of characters.

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:56.440
Shrek 5

00:10:56.440 --> 00:11:02.790
Shrek 5 won't hit theaters until nearly nine
years after Shrek Forever After, but Dreamworks

00:11:02.790 --> 00:11:06.270
is assuring viewers it will be totally worth
the wait.

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:11.260
The fifth film is apparently set to launch
a reinvented Shrek franchise, with a whole

00:11:11.260 --> 00:11:14.310
potential Shrek universe on the way as well.

00:11:14.310 --> 00:11:19.120
Screenwriter Michael McCullers said, "there's
been four movies and a lot of material, so

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:23.860
the characters are pretty beloved and they're
great characters, but you also have to think

00:11:23.860 --> 00:11:26.260
of a pretty new take at that point."

00:11:26.260 --> 00:11:30.860
While it's unclear exactly what that reinvention
will entail, it will be pretty interesting

00:11:30.860 --> 00:11:35.450
to see which fairy tale myths the franchise
decides to mine next.

00:11:35.450 --> 00:11:37.140
The Batman

00:11:37.140 --> 00:11:42.110
Right now, the big story around The Batman
comes from the movie's numerous delays.

00:11:42.110 --> 00:11:46.420
But if you look past all the negative talk,
the film is actually shaping up to be pretty

00:11:46.420 --> 00:11:47.420
good.

00:11:47.420 --> 00:11:51.480
Ben Affleck may not have dissolved into the
role of Bruce Wayne as well as Christian Bale

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:54.610
did, but he's been improving with every appearance.

00:11:54.610 --> 00:11:58.600
With a turn in Justice League coming up, he'll
hopefully have more time to settle into the

00:11:58.600 --> 00:12:01.800
character and to develop his own caped crusader.

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:07.680
Cloverfield's Matt Reeves is also set to direct,
and the script also reportedly recently underwent

00:12:07.680 --> 00:12:13.000
a rewrite from an Oscar winner, with Argo
and Justice League writer Chris Terrio turning

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:17.000
in a draft that everyone is "very happy" with.

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:19.360
Hopefully they'll find a way to squeeze some
of this in:

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:28.580
Thanks for watching!

00:12:28.580 --> 00:12:31.110
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:12:31.110 --> 00:12:33.600
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

